|~ `::builtin`, the kind of a descriptor, and the refusals of the kernel
   no reader reaches by a query: the table of primitives, the tree the
   evaluator does not know, the session, the printer and the loading of
   the catalog. ~|

::builtin
  |~~ The descriptor, a map of fields under this tag. A built-in verb
      ends its head with one, `::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/add}`, which
      names the primitive the head calls; a kind declares its
      constructor with one, `::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/vec}`; a tag
      declared with a doc alone holds an empty one. A descriptor is
      data and runs nothing by itself: a name bound to one reads it.

      ~(::builtin{:impl :qlang/prim/count} | :c / | [1 2] | c | /impl | eq :qlang/prim/count)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{:impl :qlang/type/builtin}

::BuiltinPayloadNotMapError
  |~~ `::builtin` holds the fields of a declaration as a map,
      `::builtin{:impl …}`; a payload of another kind is refused.

      ~(
        ::builtin"hello"
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::BuiltinPayloadNotMapError ::string]
       )
      ~(
        ::builtin[1 2 3]
        !| [type /actualType]
        |  eq [::BuiltinPayloadNotMapError ::vec]
       )
  ~~|

::UnknownAstNodeTypeError
  |~~ The evaluator met a node of the parser's tree it has no rule for:
      a defect of the runtime, and no failure of the query.
  ~~|

::UnknownCombinatorKindError
  |~~ The evaluator met a combinator it has no rule for: a defect of the
      runtime, and no failure of the query.
  ~~|

::PrimitiveKeyAlreadyBoundError
  |~~ Two modules of the runtime bound one primitive name, a defect of
      the runtime found as it loads.
  ~~|

::ThrowSiteSpecAlreadyRecordedError
  |~~ Two sites of the runtime declared one refusal under one name, a
      defect of the runtime found as it loads: the name is the identity
      the page and the `spec` of the refusal read, so one site would
      speak for both.
  ~~|

::PrimitiveKeyNotStringError
  |~~ A module of the runtime bound a primitive under a name that is no
      string, a defect of the runtime found as it loads.
  ~~|

::PrimitiveKeyUnboundError
  |~~ The `:impl` of a declaration names a primitive no module bound: a
      verb or a kind declared by a module whose implementation was not
      handed with it.
  ~~|

::PrimitiveRegistrySealedError
  |~~ The table of primitives is sealed when the bootstrap completes,
      and a primitive bound after it is refused.
  ~~|

::NumberNotFiniteLeakedToPrintError
  |~~ A qlang Number is a finite double. Source cannot mint an
      infinity or a NaN — the parser refuses the literal and every
      arithmetic site answers an error of its domain — so this tag
      reports a value a host installed. The print and the JSON of the
      boundary are where such a value shows: the print would be
      `Infinity`, which no literal reads back, and JSON would write
      `null`. `:actualValue` carries the offending magnitude
      as a String, the one shape that renders.
  ~~|

::BootstrapCatalogNotLoadedError
  |~~ The root of the catalog answered an error, so a module of the
      catalog the locator resolved did not load; `:tagName` names what
      the root answered with.
  ~~|

::BootstrapRootMissingError
  |~~ `#qlang/core` resolved to nothing, so the bootstrap has no
      root module to evaluate. The host adds the entry to
      `package.json#imports` (Node) or to the import map (browser),
      or hands `langRuntime({ locator })` a locator of its own.
  ~~|
